{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And He spoke.</b> It is an expression of harshness, as in ״וַיְדַבֵּר אִתָּם קָשׁוֹת״ (Genesis 42)." "<b>Go, descend.</b> From your greatness — I gave you greatness only for their sake (Berakhot 32). At that moment Moses was suspended from the heavenly court (Tanchuma)." "<b>Your people has corrupted.</b> Not 'the people' is said, but 'your people' — the mixed multitude that you accepted on your own authority and converted them without consulting Me. You said, it is good that converts cleave to the Shekhinah — they are the ones who corrupted and caused corruption (Exodus Rabbah)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:07.125048616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}